144	\begin{remark}[Good-strategy characterization]\label{rem:good-strat-characterization}
145		Using notation which will be introduced in Chapter~\ref{chap:preliminaries} below, a symmetric strategy is $(\eps,\delta,\gamma)$-good if and only if it satisfies the following three conditions. For $\ell$ and $u$ as in the axis-parallel lines test,
146		\[
147			A_a^u \ot I \simeq_\eps I \ot B^\ell_{[f(u)=a]},
148			\quad
149			\text{and}
150			\quad
151			A_a^u \ot I \simeq_\delta I \ot A_a^u.
152		\]
153		And for $\ell$ and $u$ as in the diagonal lines test,
154		\[
